  "ref": "ACT.10.10",
  "review_notes": [
    "The ASV inverts ἐγένετο ἐπ' αὐτὸν ἔκστασις to 'he fell into a trance'; αὐτόν takes the English subject and ἔκστασις the prepositional complement. Giving 'he' to ἐγένετο as a supplied subject and leaving αὐτόν to a separate word is the competing reading, but no English token would then answer to αὐτόν."
